tion. T.H.B. and J.E.H. contributed to study concept and design and to statistical support. I.P.H., H.M.B., L.V.W., and M.D.T. contributed to study concept and design. All authors, including those whose initials are not listed above, contributed to critical review and editing of the manuscript and approved the final version of the manuscript.</p><h3 class="c-article__sub-heading" id="corresponding-author">Corresponding author</h3><p id="corresponding-author-list">Correspondence to
                <a id="corresp-c1" aria-label="email Michael H. Cho" href="mailto:remhc@channing.harvard.edu">Michael H. Cho</a>.</p></div></div></section><section data-title="Ethics declarations"><div class="c-article-section" id="ethics-section"><h2 class="c-article-section__title js-section-title js-c-reading-companion-sections-item" id="ethics">Ethics declarations</h2><div class="c-article-section__content" id="ethics-content">
              
                <h3 class="c-article__sub-heading" id="FPar1">Competing interests</h3>
                <p>M.H.C., E.K.S., L.V.W., M.D.T., D.A.L., and I.P.H. have received grant funding from GlaxoSmithKline (GSK). E.K.S. has received honoraria from Novartis for continuing medical education seminars and travel support from GSK. I.P.H. has received grant support from BI. R.T.-S. is an employee and shareholder of GSK. J.V. has received personal fees from GSK, Chiesi Pharmaceuticals, BI, Novartis, and AstraZeneca. D.L.D. has received grants from the National Institutes of Health for research on COPD and personal fees from Novartis. D.A.L. has received honoraria from GSK and chaired the Respiratory Therapy Area Board from 2012 to 2015. Outside the submitted work, L.L. reports expert consultation for Boehringer Ingelheim and Novartis and unrestricted grants from AstraZeneca and Chiesi.</p>
              
